hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-17 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-17 = cons "*Activity* and *active* go back to *agere*; *hyper* is over and beyond. *Hyperactive* was made a diagnosis, a word for a child who moves too much for a classroom. The classroom is the carpenter's square again. In the old words, the hyperactive one drives beyond; in the kernel, the active pair is where anything happens at all. The diagnosis took the most generative word in the system and made it a deficit. Naming this foundation *hyperactivity* reclaims the word at its root: driving beyond, between, and together — what Lafont's interaction net does at every step, and what an unsuppressed mind does." (cons "" (cons "*Singular* returns at the end because the seed is singular. One kernel, one reaction, one root for *same* and *simple* and *singular*. *Simple* is *sem* + *plek*, folded once. A simple thing is folded once; a complex thing, *com* + *plectere*, is braided together. *Perplex* is braided through. The work's design is simple in the oldest sense: everything is folded once around one root, and the complexity is the braiding of that one fold with itself. The interaction net is a braid. DNA is a braid. Text is a weave. A language of languages is the braid of tongues. Hyperactive Interaction is the name for the fold that, folded once more, is everything else." nil))
